# 65. Project Task Catalog

---

# 1. Purpose

The Project Task Catalog is the authoritative register of all implementation work within the Loyalty Platform project.

Unlike the Product Backlog, which organizes work at a planning level, the Project Task Catalog tracks every implementation task throughout its lifecycle.

It serves as the single source of truth for:

- implementation tasks;
- AI agent assignments;
- dependency tracking;
- implementation progress;
- delivery history;
- implementation evidence.

Every implementation task executed by either a human engineer or an AI agent must exist in this catalog.

---

# 2. Scope

The Project Task Catalog contains:

- implementation tasks;
- technical tasks;
- refactoring tasks;
- migration tasks;
- testing tasks;
- documentation tasks;
- release tasks.

It does not contain:

- Product Ideas;
- Product Decisions;
- ADRs;
- Blueprint documents.

---

# 3. Principles

The Task Catalog follows these principles:

- Every task has one owner.
- Every task belongs to one module.
- Every task references Blueprint.
- Every task references Engineering.
- Every task is independently reviewable.
- Every task is independently testable.
- Every task is independently traceable.
- Every completed task leaves implementation evidence.

---

# 4. Relationship with Other Documents

The Task Catalog is built upon:

- 62-product-backlog.md
- 64-module-implementation-packages.md

Tasks are generated from the Product Backlog and executed using the corresponding Module Implementation Package.

---

# 5. Task Identifier

Every implementation task receives a permanent identifier.

Format:

```
LP-000001
LP-000002
LP-000003
```

Identifiers are sequential.

Identifiers are never reused.

Cancelled tasks remain permanently reserved.

